fixture dash_cancel_keeps_earlier_attack
doc (movement review 4, L1) Combat checklist "Dash cancels an attack on frame 4 and the cancel never eats the next attack input"; docs/adr/0010 Dash Cancels "an attack pressed before it stays buffered and fires on the dash's frame 6". Side 1 on frame 0, the next attack pressed on side 1's frame 2 (waiting for the chain at f 6), the dash on side 1's frame 6: the dash cancels the strike, the attack waits for dash frame 6 (frame 10), by then 9 frames old, and never comes out.
room test/flat
spawn 200 544
frames 30
input
  0 !attack
  1 !attack
  2..4
  5 dash
  6..29
end
expect
  at 0 action=side1
  at 5 event.dash=1 state=dash action=none
  mark slash 6..29 event.attack=1
  at slash action=side2
end
